<title>SPAIN: Spain's Andalusia auctions 10 bln pesetas.</title>
<headline>Spain's Andalusia auctions 10 bln pesetas.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Andalusia regional government (Junta de Andalucia) allotted on Thursday in a public auction a total of 10 billion pesetas in three-, five- and 10-year bonds, the regional government said  FRRD.</p>
<p>The allocation took place with a slight reduction in yields compared with the previous auction in December.</p>
<p>(amount in billions pesetas)</p>
<p>    ISSUE	    YIELD   PVS    PRICE   PVS    BID ALLOCATION</p>
<p>    7.00% NOV 99   5.567   6.131  105.10  102.60  22.9    3.0</p>
<p>    7.10% FEB 02   6.126   6.475  103.85  101.25  17.6    1.5</p>
<p>    7.25% APR 07   6.925   7.096  101.00   99.60  17.8    5.5</p>
<p>NOTE - All are tranches of old bonds. The previous auction was held on December 5.</p>
<p>Moody's long term debt rating for Junta de Andalucia is Aa3. At the end of September 1996 the region's total debt was 767 billion pesetas of which 268 billion pesetas was in bonds.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
